CORE
main.c
--no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 2
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^split small choices
^warning: ignoring
--
The rest of main after the choice of j starts a thread (through
pthread_create): a split would start one thread per copy, so main is not
split. j == 0 lets the thread overwrite slot[0] after the store of main, failing
the assertion.
